# Copy to .env and adjust. Everything here is optional.

# Where the app listens. Keep 127.0.0.1 unless you really mean to expose it.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=4750

# Your data lives in a data repository of its own, apart from this code: make one with
# `npm run init-data -- ~/dev/finance-data`, which prints these lines (docs/SELF_HOSTING.md).
# FINANCE_DATA_DIR is required in production; without it, development uses ./data, and the demo
# ./demo-data (gitignored).
# FINANCE_DATA_DIR=/home/you/dev/finance-data/data
#
# The work area (uploads waiting for review, job state, the audit log; never in git) and the inbox
# default to the data repository, beside data/: .work/<name> and inbox/.
# FINANCE_WORK_DIR=/home/you/dev/finance-data/.work/live
#
# Folder watched for new files to ingest. Point it at a Syncthing / cloud-sync folder that your
# phone saves screenshots into and they will be picked up automatically.
# FINANCE_INBOX_DIR=/home/you/dev/finance-data/inbox

# Login: one user, signed in one of two ways. Without a login the app answers direct local requests
# only, and it refuses to listen on a non-loopback HOST.
# FINANCE_USERNAME=
# FINANCE_SESSION_SECRET=
#
# a) A password. Set these with `npm run set-password`, which stores only a scrypt hash.
# FINANCE_PASSWORD_HASH=
#
# b) An OpenID Connect provider (docs/SELF_HOSTING.md, "Sign-in"). Setting the client id turns it on
#    and password sign-in off; the issuer is then required. A verified address on the list signs in
#    as FINANCE_USERNAME.
# FINANCE_OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com
# FINANCE_OIDC_NAME=Example ID      # what "Sign in with …" says (default: the issuer's host)
# FINANCE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# FINANCE_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FINANCE_OIDC_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com
# FINANCE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=      # default: https://<first FINANCE_ALLOWED_HOSTS>/api/auth/oidc/callback

# Extra Host header values to accept (comma-separated), e.g. a Tailscale MagicDNS name.
# FINANCE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=my-desktop.tailnet-name.ts.net

# Optional: use the Anthropic API for extraction instead of your logged-in `claude` CLI.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: a live feed of one Invest or Stocks ISA account's value and holdings at Trading 212, read
# from Trading 212's API: every few seconds while the app is open, less often otherwise. Not needed
# for anything else; leave unset to keep it off. Make the key in Trading 212 (Settings → API) with
# only the permissions to read account data, the portfolio and the history, limited to this
# server's IP address. About one reading an hour is recorded as a valuation. Set it on
# the live server only: Trading 212's rate limits are per account, so two servers reading it share
# them. docs/SELF_HOSTING.md, "Trading 212 live feed".
# FINANCE_T212_API_KEY=
# FINANCE_T212_API_SECRET=
# FINANCE_T212_ENV=live                # or demo: Trading 212's practice-money service, to try it out
# FINANCE_T212_ACCOUNT=                # the app's account id, or Trading 212's account number (only its
#                                      # last 4 digits are kept); default: the open Trading 212 account
#                                      # whose last 4 digits match the one the key reads
# FINANCE_T212_WATCHED_SECONDS=15      # while a page of the app is open (at least 5)
# FINANCE_T212_BACKGROUND_MINUTES=15   # otherwise, weekdays 07:00–22:00 UK time
# FINANCE_T212_QUIET_MINUTES=180       # nights and weekends
